 "title": "Evergreen FS | Evergreen FS",
 "text": "Evergreen FS | Evergreen FS Your Privacy Choices\nWe and our vendors use technology that collects data about your use of our site so we can improve and personalize our products and services, for analytics and marketing, and to fulfill your requests. We may also share this information with marketing vendors, social media companies, and analytics partners. By using our website, you acknowledge and agree to our Terms of Use. To learn more about our privacy practices review our Privacy Policy . P lease review your choices.\nDo Not Sell or Share My Personal Information\nSkip to Main Content FS Cooperatives\nContact Us\nOur Locations\nCareers\nNew Customer App\nEmployee Log In\nmyFS Log In\nAgriculture Agronomy\nCorn\nSoybeans\nForages\nWheat\nTechnology\nCrop Protection\nCrop Nutrients\nAdjuvants\nPlant Performance\nFS Agri-Finance\nEnergy\nAgricultural Propane\nFuels & Additives\nLubricants\nEnergy Equipment\nAll Ag Services\nAgriculture\nCommercial Energy\nCommercial Propane\nFuels & Additives\nLubricants\nEnergy Equipment\nFAST STOP Fuel Stations\nCustom Turf\nLawn & Tree Care\nTurf Seeds\nTurf Management\nMore Turf Products\nMore Solutions\nFS Farmtown\nAll Commercial Services\nCommercial\nResidential Energy\nResidential Propane\nFAST STOP Fuel Stations\nCustom Turf\nLawn & Tree Care\nTurf Seeds\nTurf Management\nMore Turf Products\nMore Solutions\nFS Farmtown\nAll Residential Services\nResidential\nNews Resources News\nmyFS Solution Center\nAbout Us About Us\nCareers\nSustainability\nNominate for Employee of the Month\nYour browser does not support the video tag.\nWe’re Celebrating 100 YEARS!\nLearn More\nYOUR ONE LOCAL SUPPLIER\nBuilding successful business partnerships with customers, employees, and cooperative owners in the Illinois counties of DeWitt, Livingston, Macon, McLean, and Woodford, and in the Michigan counties of Gratiot, Clinton, Genesee, Ingham, Ionia, Isabella, Livingston, Mecosta, Midland, Montcalm, Saginaw, and Shiawassee.\nAGRONOMY\nHigh-yield seed solutions, technology, crop protection, and crop nutrients.\nPropane\nReliable energy for farms, homes, and businesses.\nFuels\nPremium fuels and lubricants to keep you running.\nGrain\nGrain harvesting and marketing.\nCustom Turf\nRely on us for your lawn and tree care.\nAgri-Finance\nConvenient financing for all FS products you use in your crop production cycle.\nShowing slide 1 of 5 slides\nPROPANE\nEmergency Number for Propane\n(877) 395-4324 is our AFTER HOURS number for propane emergencies. During normal business hours, call your salesperson or main office at (877) 963-2392.\nFS Grain\nFS Grain Announcement\nEvergreen FS transferred grain assets to FS Grain effective September 1, 2026, becoming part of a strong Retail Grain Unit network.\nGAPS FS\nEvergreen FS Aquired GAPS FS\nWe’re excited to announce Evergreen FS has acquired GAPS FS, a successful agronomy company headquartered in Ithaca, Michigan, effective January 1, 2026!\nCAREERS\nJoin the Evergreen FS Team\nAre you passionate about agriculture and looking to grow your career with a leading agricultural solutions provider? View our job board and apply today!\nAGRI-FINANCE\nFS Agri-Finance Program\nFS Agri-Finance is reliable and convenient financing for ALL the FS products you use in your crop production cycle. Ask your Crop Specialist for details!\nmyfs solution center\nMake the myFS Solution Center YOUR favorite place to see all your FS account details and make payments! Get the app or use the website, and get started today!\nMake secure online payments\nTrack order history\nManage services and deliveries\nLearn More\nStay Informed\nExpert Tips and Local News to Keep You Growing\nView All Articles\nShowing slides 1-3 of 3 slides\nPost-Harvest Equipment Maintenance: Tips to Avoid Downtime Next Season\nDuring post-harvest, putting your equipment away is not the end of the maintenance cycle. Post-harvest starts next season's reliability plan.\nSoybeans\nSoybean Harvest Considerations\nAs wet weather conditions continue, multiple wetting and drying cycles beyond maturity results in soybean pod sutures breaking open and the seed falling to the soil surface. These soybeans are unable to be harvested and could be a reason for lower-than-expected yields.\nAgronomy Services\nFall Nitrogen Application\nProper soil temperature combined with a forecast of downward-trending, assures you of the best chance of preserving your fall-applied anhydrous ammonia. Read about other useful practices that will help keep N available for next spring's crop.\nFind your Local Evergreen FS\nZip Code\nSearch\nBloomington - Main Office on Hershey\n402 N. Hershey Rd. P.O. Box 1367\nBloomington , IL 61702-1367\n(877) 963-2392\nAgriculture\nCommercial\nResidential\nNews & Resources\nAbout Us\nCareers\nmyFS Agronomy\nmyFS Solution Center\nSDS\nTerms of Use\nPrivacy Policy\nEmployee Log In\nBiometric Data Retention and Deletion Policy\n© Copyright 2026 GROWMARK, Inc.",
